# {{.Name}}

A Lenny agent runtime, scaffolded by `lenny runtime init`.

- Language: {{.Language}}
- Template: {{.Template}}
- Integration level: {{.IntegrationLevel}}

## Layout

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `{{.EntrypointFile}}` | Runtime entrypoint. The message handler is an echo placeholder; replace it with the agent logic. |
| `runtime.yaml` | Runtime definition (§5.1). Declares `integrationLevel: {{.IntegrationLevel}}`. |
| `Dockerfile` | Container image build. |
| `Makefile` | `build`, `test`, and `push` targets. |
| `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | CI workflow that builds, tests, and publishes the image. |

## Build and test

```
make build IMAGE={{.Image}}
make test
```

## Validate

`lenny runtime validate` checks the repository against the Runtime
Adapter Specification (§15.4) and the `runtime.yaml` contract:

```
lenny runtime validate
```

## Publish

`lenny runtime publish` pushes the image and registers the runtime with
a gateway. It requires `LENNY_API_URL` and an admin token:

```
make push IMAGE={{.Image}}
lenny runtime publish {{.Name}} --image {{.Image}}
```
